WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.950
Thinking of borrowing ten grand?

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Going for a credit union, or a bank?

3
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.100
Most of us just go with whatever we're used to…

4
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.400
…and look at one number.

5
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.500
But there are five things worth checking first.

6
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.900
Stick with me and I'll give you all five.

7
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.800
One: the rate.

8
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.100
Banks often list around seven to nine percent on ten grand.

9
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.400
Credit unions average about ten and a half,

10
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.200
but it really varies.

11
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.000
Two: what you pay back in total over three years.

12
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.000
The difference can be a few hundred euro.

13
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.500
That's real money.

14
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.000
Three: the fees.

15
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.500
The CCPC says credit union loans come with no extra fees.

16
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.000
With a bank, it's always worth asking.

17
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.600
Four: membership.

18
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.900
Credit unions usually want you to be a member,

19
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.900
and often a bit of savings behind you.

20
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Banks don't.

21
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.000
Five: the extras.

22
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.400
Credit unions can include loan protection

23
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.100
and loan interest rebates.

24
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.900
Banks can be quicker, with more products.

25
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.600
So neither one is right for everyone.

26
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.000
Compare a quote from each,

27
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
look at the total and what's included,

28
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.600
and the right one will show itself.

29
00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.700
Not sure where to start?

30
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.800
Talk to us, and we'll go through it with you.

31
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.800
Sorted.

